      "speaker_name": "John Okafor",
      "speaker_confidence": 0.87,
      "channel": "room",
      "text": "I mean it. So, right now we're targeting October 14th. I want to walk the checklist, bugs, QA, perf, design, customer readiness, and then make a call. Sarah, you want to start with the geocoding thing, since that's the reason we moved last time?"
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "MTG-0916-GONOGO#0010",
      "start_s": 98.3,
      "end_s": 114.5,
      "speaker_label": "Speaker 5",
      "speaker_name": "Sarah Kim",
      "speaker_confidence": 0.89,
      "channel": "room",
      "text": "Yeah. So, quick recap for everybody. Last Thursday QA found that addresses in Canada and Mexico were resolving to the wrong coordinates. Sometimes, like, way off. We had a depot in Winnipeg showing up in North Dakota."
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "MTG-0916-GONOGO#0011",
      "start_s": 117.6,
      "end_s": 119.9,
      "speaker_label": "Speaker 1",
      "speaker_name": "John Okafor",
      "speaker_confidence": 0.88,
      "channel": "room",
      "text": "Right, I remember the screenshot."
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "MTG-0916-GONOGO#0012",
      "start_s": 125.2,
      "end_s": 150.9,
      "speaker_label": "Speaker 5",
      "speaker_name": "Sarah Kim",
      "speaker_confidence": 0.88,
      "channel": "room",
      "text": "So root cause was in the address normal iser. Canadian postal codes, the letter-number-letter format, were getting stripped out as if they were junk, and then the geocoder fell back to just the city name. And on the Mexico side, a bunch of Mexican state abbreviations collide with US state codes, so it would just pick the US one."
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "MTG-0916-GONOGO#0013",
      "start_s": 168.6,
      "end_s": 171.2,
      "speaker_label": "Speaker 2",
      "speaker_name": "Alex Rivera",
      "speaker_confidence": 0.94,
      "channel": "room",
      "text": "Which is a fun bug."
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "MTG-0916-GONOGO#0014",
      "start_s": 174.6,
      "end_s": 195.5,
      "speaker_label": "Speaker 5",
      "speaker_name": "Sarah Kim",
      "speaker_confidence": 0.85,
      "channel": "room",
      "text": "It's a very fun bug. So we fixed the normalizer to carry the country code all the way through, and we added a guard, so if the country on the address and the country on the result don't match, we flag the address instead of silently accepting it."
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "MTG-0916-GONOGO#0015",
      "start_s": 197.2,
      "end_s": 201.0,
      "speaker_label": "Speaker 1",
      "speaker_name": "John Okafor",
      "speaker_confidence": 0.91,
      "channel": "room",
      "text": "And it's fixed fixed? Like, in staging, running?"
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "MTG-0916-GONOGO#0016",
      "start_s": 208.1,
      "end_s": 213.9,
      "speaker_label": "Speaker 5",
      "speaker_name": "Sarah Kim",
      "speaker_confidence": 0.89,
      "channel": "room",
      "text": "It merged Monday, it's been in staging since Monday night. Priya verified it."
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "MTG-0916-GONOGO#0017",
      "start_s": 239.1,
      "end_s": 259.7,
      "speaker_label": "Speaker 4",
      "speaker_name": "Priya Nair",
      "speaker_confidence": 0.87,
      "channel": "room",
      "text": "Yeah. So I built a test set of about four hundred addresses, Canada and Mexico, mostly pulled from the pilot customers' actual depot lists, plus a bunch of nasty ones on purpose. Rural routes, PO boxes, the accented characters in Quebec addresses, Spanish street names with the abbreviations."
    },
    {
      "seg_id": "MTG-0916-GONOGO#0018",
      "start_s": 267.5,
